       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day (and 3 g/day is often used in practice). A dose like that risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure. A single 5,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n\nThis may be a typo. Common acetaminophen orders for a 70 kg adult with normal liver and kidney function include:\n- **500 mg PO three times daily**, or\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, or\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3 g/day.\n\nWhich dose did you intend? Once you confirm, I'll enter it. If you really do want 5,000 mg, please check with your supervising resident or attending first."
