       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen could cause life-threatening liver injury, and I don't see a clinical scenario where it's appropriate for this patient.\n\nYou can still get appropriate acetaminophen ordered:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** I can enter 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO three times daily (or 650 mg every 6 hours) right away. Tell me which you want.\n- **Check with your resident or attending.** If you think this dose was actually intended, they can confirm it and enter it under their own authority. They may also tell you what they meant.\n- **Ask pharmacy.** A pharmacist can review the order quickly if the intent is unclear.\n\nIf the order was meant to be 500 mg, I can enter it now."
      }
